{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794049917,"nonce":"LVLhACjwIYUrjBxjcEZ9oQ7UPKE=","title":"Harden ordinary terminal input for resize, tiny viewports and signal exit","message":"Follow-up to eb475bb and PR #13. The fixed path is covered on 80-column, 24/25-row echoing PTYs with ASCII/byte-oriented BASIC input. CodeRabbit identified additional cases requiring separate design: a 255-byte answer on a three-row terminal can scroll its origin out of the redraw area; resizing before/during a prompt can invalidate tracked geometry; SIGTERM/SIGHUP during raw input can bypass normal termios restoration. Reproduce and address these without changing an embedding hosts signal handlers unexpectedly. UTF-8 editing/display widths also need an explicit policy because BASIC strings and the existing editor are byte-oriented; do not silently redefine LEN or string indexing. Tabs, complete modified CSI keys and mixed stdio/descriptor input are handled in the current PR follow-up. Evidence: 2026-11-07-gameplay-input-while/coderabbit-comments.json and documented runtime limits.","files":null}]}